  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSum of two numbers = 40\n\nProduct of two numbers = 60\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ Let the numbers be x and y.\n\n⇒ According to the question,\n\n⇒ x + y = 40\n\n⇒ xy = 60\n\n⇒ We have to find, (1)/(x)+(1)/(y)\n\n⇒ (1)/(x)+(1)/(y)=(y+x)/(xy)\n\n⇒ Putting the values, we get\n\n⇒ (1)/(x)+(1)/(y)=(40)/(60)=(2)/(3)\n\n**Therefore, the sum of the reciprocals of two numbers is (2)/(3)**.",
